# A change to a test selects that test, and the selection comes from the
# registration rather than from here: tests/gate.sh reads meson.build
# for the tests a changed file is registered as, and falls back to the
# file's own name where the registration names it through a variable.
# What is named here is the other thing such a change can break, which
# is the rule its registration has to satisfy.
# The golden pages and the manifests that record them. A manifest is
# only ever edited beside the change that moved the bytes it records, and
# that change selects its own area; what the manifest itself needs is the
# test that reads it. Left to the catch-all a one-line manifest edit
# gates on all four hundred and thirty-nine tests at both widths, which
# is the selection this table exists to avoid.
