# ---- width: what reads the object width directly
#
# The `width` area names no path. It is not a part of the tree; it is
# what the wide build runs on a gate whose change does not reach the
# layer that decides the width.
#
# Two things put a test here, and the first is a measurement rather than
# a judgement. The whole suite was run at both widths and the two
# records compared test by test: three hundred and ten tests, of which
# twenty-one say something different in the two builds. Four of those
# differ in a temporary file's name or in a millisecond count and are
# not here. Three more are the banding tests, which differ in a
# byte-per-row figure that moves with the object size; they cost between
# half a minute and six, so they are left to the batch gate and named
# here in prose rather than run on every edit -- which is the one place
# this list knowingly trades coverage for time, and it is written down
# so that the trade is visible: band-writer, band-replay-cost and
# band-campaign.
